    "title": "DirecTV to carry new BravesVision channel in 2026",
    "text": "SportsPublished: Mar. 27, 2026, 3:00 p.m.By Creg Stephenson | cstephenson@al.comThe Atlanta Braves have reached a multi-year agreement with DirecTV to carry the new BravesVision channel, it was announced Friday.BravesVision will broadcast more than 140 games in 2026, all except those set aside for national networks (NBC, ESPN, Fox/Fox Sports 1) and/or streaming packages (Apple TV, Peacock). Out-of-market consumers can continue to watch Braves games via MLB.tv.DirecTV customers in the Braves’ broadcast “territory” (which includes all of Alabama) who previously watched games on FanDuel/Bally Sports will receive BravesVision as part of their subscription starting with Friday night’s season-opener vs. the Kansas City Royals (first pitch set for 6:15 p.m.). BravesVision will air on Channel 645 on DirecTV and on Channel 1730 on U-Verse.In addition to games, BravesVision will broadcast the “Braves on Deck” pre-game show and “Braves Postgame” show. The first pre-game show broadcast is set to air at 5 p.m. Central on Friday.RECOMMENDEDIn addition, fans who live in the Braves’ market may purchase the streaming-only BravesVision package for $19.99 per month or $99.99 per year. The Braves Vision streaming package has no blackout restrictions.A select number of Braves games will also be broadcast over the air by Gray Media, which has stations in all of Alabama’s television markets. To find out where “Braves on Gray” is available in your area, click HERE.The Braves previously announced similar agreements with two major cable outlets that serve the state of Alabama: Xfinity TV and Spectrum, as well as streaming service FuboTV. Announcements regarding BravesVision and other cable, satellite and streaming providers are expected to be made in the coming days.Creg Stephenson is a sports writer for AL.com, with a primary focus on in-state college sports. He covers South Alabama and Troy athletics, and also writes in-depth historical features on a variety of topics...",
